    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d133">

                <pb facs="0214" n="98" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg98"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/462.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to Great
                            Britain to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-05-31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 31, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>If a list can be given of proposed industrial enterprises in Manchuria, and these
                    do not at all relate to railroads, Sir Edward Grey is confident there will be no
                    further objection from either Japan or Russia. Neither objects to the currency
                    reform portion of the loan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reid</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
